.env*
# ...but the committed TEMPLATES are not secrets. Two patterns are needed and
# neither covers the other: `.env-*-example` does not match `.env-example`,
# because it requires a middle segment.
#
#   .env-example               devops/grafana/
#   .env-<name>-example        devops/backup/.env-media-mirror-example
#
# Each carries every key with a __FILL_...__ placeholder, per
# documentation/secrets.md. devops/secrets.sh refuses to apply a file that still
# contains a placeholder, which makes an unsupplied value a loud failure rather
# than a silent one.
!.env-example
!.env-*-example

# Credential files downloaded from a cloud console. These carry a live client
# secret and are NOT matched by the .env* rule above, so they must be named
# explicitly. Extract the values into the neighbouring .env and delete the
# download -- the .env file is the source of truth (documentation/secrets.md).
client_secret_*.json
credentials.json
token.json
# alertmanager directory is now version-controlled
# Only ignore the secret.yaml file (tracked in root .gitignore)
